10
00:00:41,526 --> 00:00:43,217
This module covers 5 topics.

11
00:00:43,217 --> 00:00:48,228
Phospholipid bilayer structure — The phospholipid bilayer forms a flexible boundary

12
00:00:48,228 --> 00:00:50,703
with hydrophilic and hydrophobic regions.

13
00:00:50,703 --> 00:00:55,412
Selective permeability — Selective permeability controls which materials cross

14
00:00:55,412 --> 00:00:57,223
easily and which require help.

15
00:00:57,223 --> 00:01:02,114
Passive transport — Diffusion, osmosis, and facilitated diffusion move substances

16
00:01:02,114 --> 00:01:03,314
down gradients.

17
00:01:03,314 --> 00:01:07,782
Active transport — Active transport uses energy to move substances against

18
00:01:07,782 --> 00:01:08,982
gradients.

19
00:01:08,982 --> 00:01:13,812
Osmosis and cell environments — Tonicity predicts water movement and cell volume

20
00:01:13,812 --> 00:01:17,752
changes. Each topic builds on the one before it, forming a coherent explanation.

21
